deduplicate-session-index-by-id

Lane: backend

FlatPatch: deduplicate-session-index-by-id

Form: GitDiff

Segment: none

Purpose: Keep one current session-index entry per renamed thread across all naming callers.

Requires: Unit:backend/rebuild-sqlite-history-from-paginated-rollouts

Provides: Shared index writes replace every previous entry for the named thread; rename, deletion and complete-scan pruning serialize through the home directory lock and publish atomically while preserving unrelated lines and file permissions.

Boundary: Session-index path, lookup behavior, metadata failure policies and TUI title-generation rules retain their existing owners; existing legacy duplicates are removed by the separately authorized one-time data operation.

Verification: session_index::tests cover repeated rename, explicit clear, legacy duplicates, unrelated malformed lines, permissions, directory locking, open-reader snapshots, removal and cancellation.


